  "articleBody": "Nobody wants a backsplash that looks great initially but then causes headaches down the road. There are a few common slip-ups folks make that you can totally avoid with a little planning. First, don't grout that crucial joint where your backsplash meets the countertop! That spot needs flexible caulk, not rigid grout, to handle natural shifts without cracking. Skipping wall prep is another big one; your wall needs to be clean, dry, and sometimes even primed for the best adhesion. And outlets? It's easy to forget about box extenders or longer screws to ensure your cover plates fit flush after the new tile is in. Also, misjudging height around cabinets or how the layout will work with your appliances can lead to awkward cuts or an uneven look. Taking time to plan your layout and making sure your countertop is fully installed and cured beforehand are key steps. For complex layouts or if you're feeling overwhelmed, that's often a good time to bring in a professional like HH Remodeling LLC, serving Denver and the surrounding areas, to ensure a flawless finish. We can help you navigate these details and avoid those tricky mistakes.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
